{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429002,"nonce":"b+502MnjuiRcIws461iNx4YPweo=","message":"Done, and VERIFIED ON A REAL CLUSTER rather than from helm template. Chart at deploy/helm/oto/ (Chart.yaml, documented values.yaml, API+worker Deployments, Service, ConfigMap, Secret with existingSecret support, migrate Job as a pre-install/pre-upgrade hook, optional bootstrap Job, Ingress, HPA, PDB, ServiceAccount, NOTES.txt), plus a root Dockerfile (11.2 MB distroless image).\n\nObserved live on kind, item by item against acceptance criterion 31:\n- migrate hook ran BEFORE the Deployments (pod started 15:32:40, job completed :43, API/worker created :43) and applied BOTH migrators — against a dropped/recreated empty database it produced 63 tables, goose_max=37, river_versions=7 with river_job/leader/migration/notification/queue present, so the justfile's warning about goose-alone is genuinely handled;\n- /readyz returned 200 with {\"status\":\"ready\",\"schema_version\":\"00037\",\"pools\":{\"ingest_max\":5,\"general_max\":15}} — the derived 25% split, so both pool sizes are provably wired;\n- worker Running, 0 restarts, elected a River leader and ran real jobs (occurrence.reap, source.reconcile, notify.unacked_reminder, group.close);\n- no secret material in the ConfigMap or the image (grepped the whole image tarball for the password, keyring and xoxb-/xapp-);\n- helm upgrade re-ran the hook idempotently and /readyz stayed 200.\nAlso proved existingSecret with RENAMED keys, and the bootstrap hook minting a token that authenticated GET /api/v1/sources (401 unauthenticated). All six values variants pass helm lint, kubeconform -strict and kubectl apply --dry-run=server. Clusters deleted.\n\nOne real defect fixed on the way: values.yaml shipped raw_payloads: 336h — the 14-day default ADR 0024 explicitly rejected — which would have left every payload aged 14-30 days unreplayable while its dedupe keys were still live, breaking AC-36.\n\nNOT verified: Ingress and HPA behaviour (kind has no ingress controller or metrics-server); they are render + strict-schema + server-side-admission validated only.","files":null}]}